ou know forestry mining  you know it's a it's a huge warehouse of  all of the things that the world wants  and needs he hopes the province will  realize its full potential once and for  all after it emerges from its latest  financial crisis  ross lord global news st john's  newfoundland and labrador  coming up a french slackliner wows the  crowd with epic eiffel tower  entertainment  a frightening sight on the spanish  island of la palma today a volcano is  erupting shooting huge plumes of smoke  and lava into the sky authorities  immediately evacuated more than 1 000  people but spain's civil guard now says  it may need to evacuate up to 10  thousand residents  a french daredevil is taking  entertainment to new heights in paris  the 27 year old tightrope artist  thrilled thousands of onlookers along  the banks of the sen river he walked 600  meters on a slack line more than 70  meters above the ground the tightrope  star even performed some stunts along  the way  space history has been made again the  first all-amateur crew to circle the  world without an astronaut aboard has  safely returned to earth spacex founder  elon musk picked them as his first  rocket riding tourists and as jennifer  johnson reports four more flights with  paying customers are coming soon  a dragon continuing to descend the  spacex crew dragon capsule made a  splashy entrance back to earth with four  space tourists aboard inspiration four  on behalf of spacex welcome home to  planet earth your mission has shown the  world that space is for all of us  no professional astronaut was on this  trailblazing three-day trip to space  38-year-old billionaire jared isaac man  chartered the flight paying undisclosed  millions for himself and three guests  so big part of our mission here at  inspiration four is to inspire what can  be done here in space isaac man aimed to  raise 200 million dollars for st jude  children's research hospital donating  100 million himself spacex founder elon  musk donated another 50 million  one of the tourists aboard was a saint  jude physician assistant who was a bone  cancer patient at the hospital nearly  two decades ago and did some research  while in space it's been really  interesting to see how fluid shifts with  this microgravity environment and that's  something that scientists are looking at  and so we're happy to contribute with  that arsenal's journey was an  inspiration for her young cancer  patients who did a question and answer  session with the space taurus can you  fall in space since there is no gravity  i have to say that floating is  i don't know if you saw i guys called  that peanut m m floating is so much fun  what's your favorite space food  my favorite space food is pizza which i  had yesterday looks like a smooth ride  for the crew the capsule literally ran  circles around other space tourism  competitors going 161 kilometers past  the international space station and  orbiting the earth 15 times a day  and there will be more early next year  three businessmen paying 55 million  dollars each will fly to the space  station accompanied by nasa astronauts  jennifer johnson global news washington  a boxing star from the philippines is  getting ready to throw his hat into a  different ring by running for president  of his country in 2022  we are ready to rise  to the challenge of leadership  42-year-old boxer and senator manny  pacquiao accepted the nomination of his  party saying filipinos are ready for a  change of government president rodrigo  duterte who led a brutal war against  illegal drugs is constitutionally unable  to seek a second six-year term but has  accepted a vice presidential nomination  up next the federal candidate in bc  going from paralympian to politician  there may be thousands of people across  the country running in this election  hoping to become a member of parliament  but there's no one quite like josh  vandervees this week our mike armstrong  has been looking at candidates with  interesting backstories and tonight he  introduces us to the liberal candidate  in the riding of vancouver east he's a  former paralympian a man with no arms no  legs and as you'll see no limits  yes one two three  all right he isn't one to beat around  the bush  invited to speak this week to the  vancouver east end boys club josh  vanderveese opens with a question think  to yourselves what what would it be like  if you didn't have any arms and legs now  van der vees has spent a lifetime  working on breaking the ice making that  first impression to put people he meets  at ease not a bad skill to have if  you're running for office when i was a  boy i learned how to write by  holding the pen or pencil between my arm  and cheek  and writing like this  and  it's ironic because  the teachers always said i had the best  handwriting in the  class the other skill that's translated  well is what van der vees does with  things that scare him he says he was  terrified making the jump into politics  and starting this campaign  ignoring fear is just what it's all  about growth happens outside of your  comfort zone  well vandervees has lived a life outside  what most would consider a comfort zone  and he's not really a big fan of being  told he can't do something he was born  without arms and legs and with very  supportive parents developed an aversion  to limiting himself as a boy he says he  watched jean crazier and dreamed of  going into politics excellent not for  the power but for the profile the chance  to be seen and make people think  oh can the mp in my riding can he  actually get into my store  or are there stairs or you know are we  designing vehicles that work for  someone in a wheelchair like my mp  nice sure van der vee spent a decade as  a paralympian competing in bocce he won  a bronze medal in london in 2012. after  that he went to law school and as a  lawyer works with not-for-profit groups  he's married with a daughter and a  stepson and has held on to that passion  for taking on challenges his opponent  got more than 50 percent of the vote in  the last election  it's not my first uphill battle having  the odds against him doesn't seem like  something van der vee's let's get in his  way  mike armstrong global news  what an inspiration and that is global  national for this sunday night i'm nitu  garcia tonight your canada is esther  hazy saskatchewan donna friesen will be  back at the anchor desk tomorrow and she  will host our special election coverage  throughout the evening thanks for  watching have a great night  [Music]
 

